# Class QA — Knight Bar (ABSOLUTE — ALWAYS ON)

**The owner must not have to repeat:** class QA must be thorough enough that **green gate = no hand-testing every skill in F5.**

**Authoritative template:** `docs/KNIGHT_QA_GATE.md` (P3 LOCK) · **Clone scaffold:** `docs/_CLASS_QA_GATE_TEMPLATE.md` · **Process:** `docs/design/class-rollout.md` · **Planning overlay bar:** `docs/PLANNING_SKILL_QA_CHECKLIST.md`

**Parent:** `.cursor/rules/qa-after-gameplay-changes.mdc` (which suite to run) · **All classes mandatory:** `.cursor/rules/class-qa-all-classes-mandatory.mdc` (never stop at one class; never ask owner if they want full QA) · **Complements:** `.cursor/rules/global-systems-first.mdc`, `.cursor/rules/skill-global-rules.mdc`, `.cursor/rules/move-preview-intent-truth.mdc`

---

## When this rule applies

Any turn that **implements, fixes, or claims complete** a **class** (factory, skills, passives, class scenarios, `docs/<CLASS>_QA_GATE.md`, `run_<class>_qa_gate.ps1`, `live_<class>_class_test.gd`).

Class kits are **drafts** (`.cursor/rules/skill-lists-are-drafts.mdc`). Automated gates prove the current change — **never** recite owner sign-off / LOCK / “Knight is the only PASS” in replies.

---

## Definition: class LOCK (non-negotiable)

A class is **LOCK** only when **all** are true:

1. **`docs/<CLASS>_QA_GATE.md`** — full Knight-shaped doc: three tiers, meta-critic contract, global systems fidelity (Rules A/B), **coverage matrix** with every `*_factory.gd` id.
2. **Matrix:** **100% rows `PASS`** (meta-critic approved) · **0** `HARNESS_ONLY` · **0** undocumented `PLANNED` (except owner `N/A` with target phase).
3. **One scenario file per factory row** — `tests/skills/<id>_scenario.gd` or `tests/passives/<id>_scenario.gd` — each with Bible header + named global effect + base + `[+]` when factory has `upgraded_effects`.
4. **Tier 1 gate** — `.\scripts\run_<class>_qa_gate.ps1` PASS on matrix rows, not on a monolithic harness smoke alone.
5. **Tier 2 live** — `.\scripts\run_<class>_live_qa.ps1` PASS with preview/commit + **overlay tile sets** + slots + sim parity (checklist § Automated layers).
6. **`IMPLEMENTATION_STATUS.md`** — records LOCK hash; **must not** say "QA LOCK" while matrix has `HARNESS_ONLY` rows.

**Planning QA PASS is not class LOCK.** Forbidden: changing `live_planning_scene_test.gd` for class coverage.

---

## Forbidden shallow patterns (instant `HARNESS_ONLY` / not LOCK)

| Pattern | Why it fails Knight bar |
|---------|-------------------------|
| Single `*_class_scenario.gd` / harness as **only** coverage | No per-row Bible proof; one green script hides weak skills |
| Assert `ability.target_shape` / metadata only | Does not prove tiles hit or red overlay correct |
| `GridSystem.get_affected_tiles` smoke **disconnected** from ability under test | Proves enum math, not this skill at this hover |
| Sim/live: `ABILITY_USED` or any single `UNIT_DAMAGED` | Does not prove footprint, multi-target, or wrong-tile exclusion |
| Live: contract asserts only; no `overlay.get_hover_action_range_tiles()` vs blast at hover | Violates `PLANNING_SKILL_QA_CHECKLIST.md` |
| Red tiles compared to `planning_action_range_tiles()` only for AOE | Range bubble ≠ Bible blast; self-referential pass |
| Gate doc &lt; Knight structure (no matrix, no meta-critic, no tier table) | Owner cannot trust PASS |
| Mark class complete in status while matrix is `HARNESS_ONLY` | False sign-off |

---

## Required asserts (AOE / shapes / ranged)

For any skill with `target_shape` ≠ `SINGLE` or Bible `AOE` / `ARC` / `LINE` / `CONE`:

1. **Sim:** place units **in** and **out** of `GridSystem.get_affected_tiles(origin, target, shape, size)`; assert damage/status/terrain only on expected coords.
2. **Live / planning:** at scripted hover, `overlay.get_hover_action_range_tiles()` (or dedicated blast layer when implemented) must match **Bible footprint at cursor**, not Manhattan range bubble alone.
3. **Commit:** preview slots + `Simulator.simulate` agree on `target_coord` and affected tile set.

Shared geometry owner: `GridSystem.get_affected_tiles` — **no** per-skill overlay branches.

**Automated enforcement:** `.\scripts\run_aoe_footprint_qa_gate.ps1` (also wired into class + planning gates). Fails if shaped scenario rows lack sim footprint proof, live class tests lack exact overlay parity, or premove ARC regression is missing.

---

## Agent workflow (every class turn)

1. Read `docs/<CLASS>_QA_GATE.md` matrix — know which rows are `HARNESS_ONLY`.
2. New class: start from `docs/_CLASS_QA_GATE_TEMPLATE.md` (not a blank stub).
3. Per skill wave: add scenario file → register → promote row `HARNESS_ONLY` → `PASS` only after meta-critic adequacy.
4. Changelog **Class QA** line: suites run and **PASS** / **FAIL**. Do not tell the owner a class is finished.
5. Run **both** `run_<class>_qa_gate.ps1` and `run_<class>_live_qa.ps1` when class factory/scenarios/live tests change.

---

## P6 clone checklist (mandatory for new classes)

1. Copy `docs/_CLASS_QA_GATE_TEMPLATE.md` → `docs/<CLASS>_QA_GATE.md`
2. Fill matrix from `<class>_factory.gd` + `class_abilities.txt` — honest `PLANNED` / `HARNESS_ONLY`
3. Copy `run_knight_qa_gate.ps1` pattern → `run_<class>_qa_gate.ps1`
4. One `tests/skills/<id>_scenario.gd` per active; `tests/passives/<id>_scenario.gd` per passive
5. `run_<class>_live_qa.ps1` → `tests/live_<class>_class_test.gd`
6. Do **not** tell the owner a class is finished or signed off (skill lists will keep changing)
